# Vendored upstream source is imported verbatim and never edited in place. Its whitespace is the
# vendor's, and reformatting it would break the SHA256SUMS manifest that makes "has anyone edited
# upstream?" one command -- so the checks are turned off for it rather than the files cleaned up.
# `-text` for the same reason: SHA256SUMS attests bytes, so no eol conversion may touch them.
#
# Measured on the VL53L7CX import: 1,396 `git diff --check` warnings, all under these paths, none
# in our own code.
#
# Scoped to upstream and to patches deliberately. Our own Zephyr adaptation next to it --
# vl53l7cx_uld/zephyr/platform.c and friends -- is project-maintained code and stays checked.
lexxpluss_apps/third_party/st/vl53l7cx_uld/upstream/** -whitespace -text

# Patches are byte-exact by definition: an eol conversion or a stripped trailing space stops them
# applying, and `vl53l7cx_sources.cmake` fails the configure when that happens.
lexxpluss_apps/third_party/st/vl53l7cx_uld/zephyr/patches/** -whitespace -text
